  <h2 id="next-step">Your next step</h2>
  <p class="line">
    Breaking through a career plateau in India starts with an honest, layer-by-layer audit, not a resignation letter written on a bad Tuesday. Run the content check on yourself this week. Have the direct conversation with your manager before the next review cycle. If both come back clean, check the internal job board and consider a skip-level. If all three point the same way, a plan for a real external move is the sound next step, not a failure of patience. Whichever layer turns out to be the real blocker, the underlying goal is the same: keep building a high-income skill portfolio that keeps opening doors, so no single company's structure or a single manager's advocacy can cap how far you go. If you want a structured, outside opinion on which layer is actually holding you back, <a href={guidanceUrl}>career counselling and guidance</a> is built for exactly this decision, and a <a href={assessmentsUrl}>free career and skill assessment</a> is a reasonable, no-cost way to check your skill positioning before you commit further time to any one path.
  </p>

